    "Object identities, full designation sets, coordinates, apparent sizes and types were checked against the unchanged pinned OpenNGC-derived catalogue.",
    "OpenNGC supports measurement-based observing advice and month/latitude guidance, not claims about discovery or stellar physics. Practical advice is conservative editorial inference, not a report of field observations or a guaranteed aperture threshold.",
    "Difficulty labels describe first detection under suitable sky/latitude conditions, not access to photographed structure; the existing shared IT/EN/ES difficulty vocabulary is reused.",
    "Source pages were read for specific claims. Visible-light, infrared and high-resolution features are distinguished; uncertain companions, wind explanations and motion-derived ages retain qualifiers in every language.",
    "Italian is canonical. English and Spanish receive separate terminology/grammar review and side-by-side checks of numbers, qualifiers, aliases and observational limits. No catalogue measurements, recommendation flags, image seeds or scoring code are changed."
